  "worked_solution": "Since $P(x)\u21d2Q(x)\u2261\u00acP(x)\u2228Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={T}_{\u00acP\u2228Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{\u00acP}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7 & \\ge 9 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 16 \\\\ x & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=[4,\\infty ).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,4).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(0,5).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,4)\\cup (0,5) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
